00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:43.550
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So I will introduce Verana. Some of you may know a little bit about this project but I will try to summarize so that it will be easy for you to understand and we can go straight to the Governing Point.

162
00:18:43.670 --> 00:18:48.150
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So the Verona is a registry of trust registries.

163
00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:58.979
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So we believe that what we want is that any ecosystem should be able to create their own trust registry.

164
00:18:59.230 --> 00:19:17.880
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Define a governance framework, publish the governance framework, define the list of credential schema they would like to use in their ecosystem, and build a tree of accredited issuers, verifiers.

165
00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:32.800
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: and holders. So this is the first brick of Verana is a public infrastructure where anyone can create its own ecosystem and define all of them.

166
00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:40.810
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Then… We have a second brick in Verana which is the service identity.

167
00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:58.100
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: We believe that in an Agentic Internet, if there is no identity for AI agents, everybody is talking about that, but not only AI agents, any service, any connected thing, we need to know who is the controller behind this entity.

168
00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:11.520
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And at the same time, if we are able to know who is a controller of an entity, then we can mutually authenticate before trying to connect.

169
00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:19.020
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And then if we agree with the authentication, then we can connect and we can bootstrap any protocol we want.

170
00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:36.629
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So, Verona defines some specifications, based only on open standards. The verifiable trust specification that defines precisely how to authenticate services and how to authenticate.

171
00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:46.849
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: software that is participating to connection in general. So, not only services, but you can even use it in order to authenticate user agents, for example.

172
00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:57.289
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So the principle is based on a DID. Every service is identified by a DID. It is presenting some credentials.

173
00:20:57.290 --> 00:20:59.170
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: in the DID documents.

174
00:20:59.170 --> 00:21:23.619
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: using linked verifiable presentations and then the credentials are issued by some ecosystems that can be in Verana or could be in another registry of registry and at the end we decide if we trust the service by deciding if we trust the ecosystem that

175
00:21:23.620 --> 00:21:24.960
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: issues the credentials.

176
00:21:24.990 --> 00:21:30.140
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So the service identity is resolved like this in the Verana concept.

177
00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:43.939
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Because… because we… we are using a ledger to anchor the ecosystems, so the ledger is used to, to store the trust registry of the ecosystem, so we store the schemas.

178
00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:48.670
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And we store the accreditation trees.

179
00:21:48.900 --> 00:21:56.070
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And obviously no personal data, no information is stored in the ledger, only DIDs.

180
00:21:56.550 --> 00:22:14.440
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: and schemas, and then, because we have this ledger, each time there is a participant to an ecosystem, and each time this participant is presenting a public credential attached to the DID, then automatically we can build a graph.

181
00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:34.280
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So this graph is built by indexing every little service that is presenting a credential from ecosystem defined in Verana. And it could be bridged to ecosystem from other other tertiary resources.

182
00:22:34.510 --> 00:22:49.380
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So at the end, using this trust graph, we can query this graph and for example, request ask where are the verifiable services of a company, for example.

183
00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:55.569
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Or show me all the agents that are certified ISO 123.

184
00:22:55.570 --> 00:23:15.380
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: and so on. So this is what we've built with Verana. There is a testnet currently working, and all the modules that are behind the ledger, the ledger is only a very small part of the infrastructure, but at the end, anyone can create a service.

185
00:23:15.590 --> 00:23:27.000
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And then publish a DID for this service with what they are calling in Europe a business wallet. But it's a cloud agent, let's say.

186
00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:42.190
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And you attach, you join the ecosystems you want, you obtain credentials and you present the credentials in your documents. You can be accredited by several ecosystems as an issuer, as a verifier.

187
00:23:42.190 --> 00:23:52.610
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: You can create your own ecosystem, etc. So the idea that your DID finally is visible like that, the credentials they present.

188
00:23:52.750 --> 00:23:57.950
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: and the accreditation that UDID have.

189
00:24:00.260 --> 00:24:13.109
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So, how do you… how do we manage the Governance of that? By the way, I would say better how we plan to do it, because one of the reasons why we are presenting that to you

190
00:24:13.110 --> 00:24:27.330
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: It's because it's not, it's not closed yet and, and, and we must, receive feedback and, and probably help. So, we separated, we separated in two entities.

191
00:24:27.460 --> 00:24:32.879
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: the project. So we have the Verona Foundation that hosts the specification.

192
00:24:32.890 --> 00:24:48.190
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: and towards the open source software. So the Verana Foundation is only for the software and for the specification, has no governance rights on the Verana infrastructure. And then from the other side we have the Verana Council.

193
00:24:48.470 --> 00:25:06.470
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Which, goal is to govern and secure the network. So, we will, focus this, this presentation today on the Council, on the Council, because Verona Foundation is, is really for, providing the software and the specifications.

194
00:25:07.180 --> 00:25:12.550
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So… And because Verona is a registry of registries.

195
00:25:12.820 --> 00:25:18.320
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: We have a layered Governance model.

196
00:25:19.060 --> 00:25:26.529
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: The goal is to have every ecosystem, have their own governance.

197
00:25:26.710 --> 00:25:28.170
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: While we have…

198
00:25:28.730 --> 00:25:48.579
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Governance for the infrastructure itself, what we're calling the network governance. And we want this network governance to be as simple as possible and delegate all the sovereignty to the ecosystems that are building themselves in the infrastructure.

199
00:25:48.940 --> 00:26:00.199
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So let's first talk about the Ecosystem Governance because it's simpler here in this presentation.

200
00:26:00.870 --> 00:26:13.489
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Ecosystem in Verana is 100% sovereign. So they define their own rules. They can define some business models for the credentials.

201
00:26:13.490 --> 00:26:35.990
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: They can say, they can explain how to join the Ecosystem as an issuer, as a verifier, there are some fees for that. They can explain what are the risks, what are the rules, what are the sanctions if you do not respect the Governance Framework as a participant and so on. So this is

202
00:26:35.990 --> 00:26:37.810
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: 100% sovereign.

203
00:26:37.810 --> 00:26:47.209
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And the network governance cannot be part of the governance of each ecosystem. Each ecosystem is totally independent.

204
00:26:47.260 --> 00:26:58.520
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So what we want is a public infrastructure where every ecosystem is sovereign. So that's why we have this separation.

205
00:26:59.470 --> 00:27:03.650
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Now let's talk about the Governance of the infrastructure.

206
00:27:03.750 --> 00:27:13.060
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So if we want to give ecosystem a public infrastructure so they can create themselves as sovereign ecosystems.

207
00:27:13.060 --> 00:27:23.819
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Then we need to define a Governance for the network that is the more neutral possible.

208
00:27:23.820 --> 00:27:27.570
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So… What we want? We want neutrality.

209
00:27:28.570 --> 00:27:43.959
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Equality. So we don't want, for example, a member to control the governance of the infrastructure. We want openness, federalism so that all ecosystems are autonomous. Transparency.

210
00:27:44.370 --> 00:27:54.120
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: accountability, Data minimization… And obviously the principle verify, don't trust or don't trust, verify.

211
00:27:54.460 --> 00:27:58.980
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And, proportionality in case of problems.

212
00:27:59.090 --> 00:28:18.069
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: and legal safety. So, we don't want, we don't want someone to take over, the Governance of the Council because of money. We don't want, someone, to take a position on the Council for, for, for…

213
00:28:18.700 --> 00:28:25.469
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Politic, politic decisions. So we want something the most neutral possible.

214
00:28:26.600 --> 00:28:40.689
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So what we defined and that is pending, it's just a draft. So it is pending a better definition is a nonprofit Swiss association for the council.

215
00:28:41.400 --> 00:28:49.190
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Where we have a small board with zero network authority and we have one member, one vote.

216
00:28:49.520 --> 00:29:04.729
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And each member runs a ledger node because finally the ledger is the only part that needs to be run by a selected council. All the other modules can be deployed and run by anyone.

217
00:29:04.910 --> 00:29:24.009
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So we want the council to be a free membership because we don't want any barrier based on money. Of course, we want a regional balance. So we don't want all council members to be from the same region or from the same sector.

218
00:29:24.160 --> 00:29:43.709
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And what we don't want, we don't want a capture. So we cannot have, for example, a single entity that has subdivision and every subdivision is a member of the council and at the end they are controlling the council. So we don't want that.

219
00:29:43.940 --> 00:29:55.020
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And we want to have public sector observers that can see what's happening in the Council.

220
00:29:56.950 --> 00:30:21.460
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So concretely in terms of what the council do does, of course they are building the Governance Framework documents. That's the first topic. It's written here in small, but that's the first topic. They execute the nodes and they

221
00:30:21.520 --> 00:30:38.210
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: take decisions, devote for taking decisions that are really just to maintain and to make the infrastructure, up and running properly, and, preventing, from, I mean,

222
00:30:38.210 --> 00:30:42.780
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Brutal changes or things that could alter the business and the stability of the infrastructure.

223
00:30:43.170 --> 00:30:54.460
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So they cannot, they cannot, the council cannot, I mean, contribute or take a decision in an ecosystem. This is not possible.

224
00:30:54.460 --> 00:31:09.549
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: They cannot alter, for example, the farms, if there are farms in some ecosystem, or they cannot alter the behavior of an ecosystem just because they want to do so. This is not possible.

225
00:31:12.290 --> 00:31:30.060
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: By the way, every ecosystem has its own rules and they have, they even can apply sanctions, but this is their own rules and the council has no way to alter, to, to take part on, on, on the, on the ecosystem, governance.

226
00:31:30.730 --> 00:31:43.319
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So I don't want to enter a lot into the details of how the economic model is working in Verana because it will be too deep for this session.

227
00:31:43.430 --> 00:31:52.239
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: What you have to understand is that the more you are using, you are joining Ecosystem and you are participating to Ecosystem.

228
00:31:52.240 --> 00:32:04.589
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: The more you pay transactions because, for example, Ecosystem decided that the verification of a credential costs money. So each time there are some trust fees that are being paid.

229
00:32:04.610 --> 00:32:22.320
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: then there is a trust deposit that is minted for the one that is paying, and for the one that is receiving a commission. This trust deposit is used as a stake for a proper…

230
00:32:22.570 --> 00:32:28.310
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: I mean, behavior of the, of the participants.

231
00:32:29.460 --> 00:32:33.970
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: related to the Governance Framework. If the participant is properly

232
00:32:34.380 --> 00:32:46.580
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: respecting the Governance Framework of an ecosystem, then as soon as they start to use the ecosystem and contribute by doing some payments, for example, their trust deposit increases.

233
00:32:46.580 --> 00:32:54.849
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And then if for some reason they decide to do something wrong and they are not respecting the Governance Framework, then the ecosystem.

234
00:32:54.850 --> 00:33:07.689
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: can apply a sanction by slashing their trust deposit, which means that they will have a Red Cross and if they want to join another ecosystem, for example, they will see that.

235
00:33:07.690 --> 00:33:20.660
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: they have been slashed by another ecosystem, so maybe the second ecosystem will not want to accept them to join, because they will see the slash. So, this is a kind of…

236
00:33:20.660 --> 00:33:35.480
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: of mechanism in order to make sure that participants wants to respect the governance framework and to enforce the governance framework.

237
00:33:35.820 --> 00:33:51.569
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So then this trust deposit can be used by the network in case of a problem. We will see that later with a participant of the network.

238
00:33:52.420 --> 00:34:10.240
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So this is this slide precisely. So let's say for example the Council, the Network Governance receive for example a notification saying that this organization in this country is doing something wrong.

239
00:34:10.239 --> 00:34:20.790
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Or if the Governance detects that, receive a report from someone that this organization is doing something wrong.

240
00:34:20.800 --> 00:34:28.040
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So, the Council can analyze until some point, and can, and can try to solve

241
00:34:28.040 --> 00:34:49.449
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: the issue with the organization. And in some really rare cases, they could slash the trust deposit of the bad actor. And in this case, when you have your trust deposit slashed in an ecosystem.

242
00:34:49.449 --> 00:35:06.359
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: then, all your trust operations on this ecosystem are paused. But if you are being slashed by the network governance, then all your, all your participation in all ecosystems are paused until you, you, replenish your trust deposit. So.

243
00:35:06.470 --> 00:35:12.600
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: The Governance is not the Governance framework.

244
00:35:13.050 --> 00:35:15.290
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Of the network.

245
00:35:15.460 --> 00:35:23.800
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: We will not give to the Network Governance the power to disable an ecosystem because we don't want that or disable an organization.

246
00:35:23.820 --> 00:35:42.070
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: But they can, in an extreme cause, slash the bad actor, and in this case, the bad actor is suspended. So, of course, as soon as they have been suspended, they cannot operate anymore until they replenish the trust deposit.

247
00:35:42.430 --> 00:36:05.880
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So regarding the day-to-day governance, each time there is the need of doing some change, for example to the network Governance Framework or an update of the software for the node of the ledger, then we publish Governance

248
00:36:07.650 --> 00:36:24.640
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Governance proposal. Sorry. And then, we vote and then the Governance proposal pass if we have the 66% and there is an emergency fast path in case of something really, really, urgent.

249
00:36:24.880 --> 00:36:29.589
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: But, at the end,

250
00:36:29.760 --> 00:36:52.560
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: The members are acting in a day to day with 30 days public comment until the proposal pass. All the ledger nodes must run with software which is AGPL3. That's one of the things we are proposing. Why? Because we don't want some nodes to run

251
00:36:52.560 --> 00:36:53.989
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Obscure,

252
00:36:54.140 --> 00:37:17.550
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: code we want everything to be fully verifiable so the principle don't trust verify apply not only to the business the credential and so on but to the code of the of what is running in the ledger so that's why we want to enforce the the ledger nodes to be a gpu3 in order to

253
00:37:17.610 --> 00:37:18.720
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Guarantee that.

254
00:37:19.940 --> 00:37:23.120
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So, what's…

255
00:37:23.120 --> 00:37:46.329
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Is the status of what's of the building of the council. So at the moment we are just starting. So we have some candidates that are interested in helping and joining the council. For now, we are waiting. We have not selected anyone because we want to have more choice first.

256
00:37:46.460 --> 00:38:00.920
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And second, we still need to work on the governance frameworks. So that's why at the moment we will not choose. But there are some interesting candidates already.

257
00:38:00.920 --> 00:38:12.109
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And we must continue to work on the Governance and we need feedback for what we have done until now.

258
00:38:12.170 --> 00:38:23.149
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So, yeah, I think that everything is public so you can access the documentation. You can see the document we start to build.

259
00:38:23.330 --> 00:38:30.130
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And, yeah, of course, as I was explaining, no technical stuff in this…

260
00:38:30.130 --> 00:38:43.830
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: in this presentation. Of course we are aligned with all standard specifications. We are Trusted Registry Query Protocol compatible so you can query any ecosystem using the TRQPv2.

261
00:38:43.830 --> 00:39:06.310
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: protocol, and yeah, so we are really eager to have your feedback and to see if someone wants to contribute, because at the end, this is a public infrastructure that we even won't own. I mean, it's for everybody, and so everyone that wants to contribute, to join, to

262
00:39:06.310 --> 00:39:16.739
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: To help us or to give feedback is welcome. So that's all for now. Now I would like to have your questions or comments.

263
00:39:16.870 --> 00:39:19.989
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And see what you're thinking.

264
00:39:23.150 --> 00:39:24.850
Steven Milstein: Cool. Very nice.

265
00:39:25.630 --> 00:39:27.150
Steven Milstein: Anybody have any questions?

266
00:39:30.740 --> 00:39:33.300
Steven Milstein: I do have one to start, sorry, Drummond.

267
00:39:33.300 --> 00:39:35.069
Drummond Reed (First Person Cooperative): No, no, go ahead, start.

268
00:39:35.070 --> 00:39:44.949
Steven Milstein: Yeah. So I'm curious about the business model. Like, how is this self-sustaining? I know you didn't want to get into the technical details, but I'm just from a…

269
00:39:45.270 --> 00:39:47.619
Steven Milstein: How does the network maintain itself?

270
00:39:48.500 --> 00:40:02.680
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Okay that's a good point. So let me give you the general concepts we are how we do develop the business on Verana. So first on the

271
00:40:02.890 --> 00:40:16.170
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: on the Verona network, there is a token that is issued when we launch a mainnet. But the token is not to build a speculative business. The token is only used.

272
00:40:16.260 --> 00:40:31.910
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: In order so that when there are trust fees to be paid in ecosystem, let's say, for example, you want to verify your credential from an ecosystem and the ecosystem says you need to pay $1 for this verification.

273
00:40:31.970 --> 00:40:38.359
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So the ecosystem chooses its price point, $1.

274
00:40:39.000 --> 00:40:44.679
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: From this $1 that you will need to pay, you will need to have 5%.

275
00:40:44.810 --> 00:40:49.310
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: To found your trust deposit so this 5%.

276
00:40:49.530 --> 00:40:52.180
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: You will need to pay the 5%,

277
00:40:52.230 --> 00:40:56.020
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: in the token of the chain in VNA.

278
00:40:56.050 --> 00:41:11.249
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And you will use this VANA to pay you 5%. You will pay the $1 in fiat, but you will mint trust unit using this 5% of the token of the blockchain.

279
00:41:11.250 --> 00:41:16.099
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And this 5% that are used to mint your trust deposit.

280
00:41:16.100 --> 00:41:25.390
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: are used to the network validator which are the council members. So the council members they have

281
00:41:25.550 --> 00:41:32.139
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: a cap specified in dollars, in US dollars per month for running a node.

282
00:41:32.380 --> 00:41:51.350
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So as soon as they have not reached the cap, every time there is a trust fee transaction, that means the trust deposit, the 5% is used, is converted to USD and used to pay the council members.

283
00:41:51.520 --> 00:42:09.239
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: when we already, reached the cap for the council member, then the, VNA, the corresponding VNA are burned. So, which means we have a deflationary, tokenomics. So that's for the, how the network is working.

284
00:42:09.280 --> 00:42:17.400
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: The trust units of your trust deposits are decaying over time. So, for example, if you participate actively to an ecosystem.

285
00:42:17.670 --> 00:42:33.380
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Then you will have a certain number of trust units. The trust units are not convertible. So when you have trust units in your deposit, you will see this organization, they have 20, they are worth 20 K US dollar trust units.

286
00:42:33.550 --> 00:42:44.239
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And so over the time, this trust unit decays. And if you are not actively using the network, your trust deposit value is reduced.

287
00:42:44.430 --> 00:43:09.299
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: But these trust units are only an information of how frequently you are using the ecosystems and what is your weight in the ecosystems. But that's not the business model that will make you earn money with Verana. What makes you earn money with Verana is when you build your ecosystem, you define your business model on your ecosystem.

288
00:43:09.300 --> 00:43:10.000
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: system.

289
00:43:10.210 --> 00:43:30.109
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And you charge third parties for, for example, for credentials. Or you charge third party for onboarding. Okay, so these, these are the business model, that, that, you can enforce on each ecosystem. And at the end, we, as, as Verana.

290
00:43:30.170 --> 00:43:43.980
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So I am one of the founders of Verona, but at the same time I have companies. One of the companies is called 2060, for example, and we are building a solution, a SaaS solution.

291
00:43:44.120 --> 00:43:55.789
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: For selling business wallets. So we will start probably in the European Union because it's something that is really on time.

292
00:43:55.860 --> 00:44:05.940
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And what we are providing these business wallets are integrated to Verana. So you can work for example with with European Trust List and at the same time.

293
00:44:06.010 --> 00:44:25.359
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: you can create or join ecosystems that are private ecosystems that are not managed by governments, that are not in the European Union trustees, for example, and then you can monetize ecosystems, you can pay for ecosystems if you need something, but at the end.

294
00:44:25.630 --> 00:44:27.560
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: You can build services.

295
00:44:27.740 --> 00:44:40.160
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: that enable third party to access all this universe of creating an ecosystem, a joint ecosystem, etc. So to give you an example of what we can build.

296
00:44:40.420 --> 00:44:47.289
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: At the moment in a Latin America country, we are building a business registry.

297
00:44:47.690 --> 00:45:03.980
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So that, you have, you have all organizations that are identified by your DID, and then they can join Ecosystems to obtain credentials and present the credential in their DA documents, and automatically they appear on the trust graph.

298
00:45:03.980 --> 00:45:16.100
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So then you can search for example, the European passport of or for example, who is exporting shoes and has a European passport in Peru, for example.

299
00:45:16.640 --> 00:45:23.849
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: You see, so this, this, this, these business models are independent per ecosystem.

300
00:45:24.110 --> 00:45:32.699
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: And the blockchain NC is not to generate money with the infrastructure. This is not the purpose.

301
00:45:32.960 --> 00:45:42.989
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: By the way, when we launch the mainnet, even the council member gets because there is a token that is issued, all the participants got a part of the token.

302
00:45:43.090 --> 00:45:55.680
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: So the token is not what makes the business interesting. What makes the business interesting is that anyone can use the infrastructure to build the ecosystem and monetize.

303
00:45:56.810 --> 00:46:14.149
Steven Milstein: Okay, one quick follow-up, then I'll let the others go. So you mentioned, so tokens are used to support the infrastructure, great, and that ecosystems can charge whatever they want, you know, to issue a credential, to verify credentials, and so on. And you said that was in regular fiat?

304
00:46:15.170 --> 00:46:15.850
Fabrice Rochette - Verana.io: Yeah, by the way.

305
00:46:15.850 --> 00:46:18.710
Steven Milstein: How do you take… how do you take 5% of

306
00:46:19.400 --> 00:46:29.500
Steven Milstein: I may charge a dollar for a verification, Scott may charge $10. How are you taking 5% in…

307
00:46:29.700 --> 00:46:30.640
Steven Milstein: tokens.

308
00:46:31.690 --> 00:46:32.130
Scott Perry (Digital Governance Institute): Oh.

309
00:46:32.130 --> 00:46:36.659
Steven Milstein: Different denominations of charges between different ecosystems.

310
00:46:36.990 --> 00:46:44.870
Steven Milstein: And how does the ecosystem settle? Are they trading actual tokens and then have to go to an exchange to get the money out?

311
00:46:44.870 --> 00:46:57.370
